.TH YES "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
yes \- output a string repeatedly until killed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yes
[\fI\,STRING\/\fR]...
.br
.B yes
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Repeatedly output a line with all specified STRING(s), or 'y'.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/yes#yes--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/yes#yes--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
